<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Turtkul</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Petro-Aleksandrovsk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Turtkul is a town on the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> in Karakalpakstan, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>. Founded as the Russian fort of Petro-Aleksandrovsk after the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khiva">Khiva</a> in 1873, it was the capital of the Karakalpak autonomous region until 1939, when erosion by the river and the growth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nukus">Nukus</a> led to the transfer of the capital.</p></div>
